There's 328 students coming up to the high school next year, 233 of them.

378
00:44:09,175 --> 00:44:16,258
So 71% of the rising freshmen class has chosen a CTE pathway, which is great.

379
00:44:16,799 --> 00:44:26,423
However, as Mr. Murphy mentioned, we are entering kind of, I would say within the next few years, we're gonna need to make, like I'm doing this year, I'm proposing additional teachers because there's the need for it.

380
00:44:27,464 --> 00:44:33,947
Also important to know that 45% of the students in grades 10 through 12 at Medford High School are now enrolled in the CTE pathway.

381
00:44:34,913 --> 00:44:37,535
So that's a major shift from what we're used to in years past.

382
00:44:38,575 --> 00:44:46,721
And it's forcing us to look at academic offerings, too, to make sure that we have a balance between programs to make sure that we have additional teachers to help.

383
00:44:47,021 --> 00:44:54,086
Where in the past, let's say we only needed three or four English teachers on the vocational side, we're going to need to look at teachers on the high school side as well.

384
00:44:54,126 --> 00:44:57,328
So it's all a good problem to have, but it is forcing us to make some decisions.

385
00:44:58,068 --> 00:45:01,869
So as I said, Grade 9, we have 233 students coming in for freshman rotation.

386
00:45:02,449 --> 00:45:04,309
Grade 10, we have 162.

387
00:45:04,829 --> 00:45:05,370
Grade 11, 136.

388
00:45:05,630 --> 00:45:07,670
And senior class of 132.

389
00:45:08,950 --> 00:45:10,411
So these numbers continue to rise.

390
00:45:10,451 --> 00:45:14,932
To give you some perspective, this year we have about 118 seniors graduating.

391
00:45:15,852 --> 00:45:20,713
So a total of 643 students are on a CTE pathway now at our lovely school.

392
00:45:20,753 --> 00:45:21,953
So we're very excited.

393
00:45:26,341 --> 00:45:38,926
So with all that said, for the past I believe three years I have asked for a level funded budget, because as Mr. Murphy mentioned I do have other sources of income, those were pretty much depleted during coven and during the shutdown.

394
00:45:39,726 --> 00:45:42,608
However, we do have the ability to generate some money, we have.

395
00:45:44,023 --> 00:45:55,994
revolving accounts for several of my programs so automotive culinary graphic design, we have programs that raise money that we can use that money gets put directly back into the program we don't use it for anything else other than those programs.

396
00:45:57,336 --> 00:46:04,022
We also have the tuition that i'm able to accept for out of district students which this year i've been working with Belmont.

397
00:46:04,573 --> 00:46:05,954
Watertown and Sudbury.

398
00:46:06,114 --> 00:46:12,400
As crazy as it may seem, Sudbury is very interested in us because they consider us a neighboring school district.

399
00:46:12,600 --> 00:46:22,949
There is a lack of seats statewide for students in vocational programming, so what we're really doing is we're doing right by students by offering them programming if they want it.

400
00:46:23,029 --> 00:46:26,813
There are many students who did not get into their vocational programming in their regional school district,

401
00:46:27,473 --> 00:46:32,437
So they've heard the good things that are happening in Medford and we've become a district of choice for those three schools.

402
00:46:33,358 --> 00:46:44,567
Ultimately, what's going to happen is we are going to have an agreement with all three towns, so that they understand when I met with them it was it was difficult because I told them I would love to help, but I also have to keep my Medford.

403
00:46:45,508 --> 00:46:48,251
family in mind and we have programs that fill up really quickly.

404
00:46:49,292 --> 00:46:56,820
The districts I'm working with are so happy that they have an option that they're willing to go into an agreement with us that basically says there are some programs that we know fill up quickly.

405
00:46:57,441 --> 00:47:05,189
My fear was that if we offer a spot to a Belmont or a Watertown or a Sudbury student and they were placed in a program that typically fills up,

406
00:47:05,990 --> 00:47:23,742
how would that feel to a medford student so they understood my concern so we're going to have an agreement going forward that basically we can offer seats to out of district students based on availability so if if we have a program that fills on medford residents then we leave it that way so we still have maintained that um as you know seats for our students

407
00:47:24,740 --> 00:47:26,101
So that's another source of income.

408
00:47:27,142 --> 00:47:35,249
I don't understand how the calculation works but I that is my goal this year to find out how the state figures out how to give us our designation for tuition.

409
00:47:36,109 --> 00:47:38,872
Last year for a school district to send a student to Medford was 12,314.

410
00:47:40,813 --> 00:47:43,876
This year, or next year, went down to $10,000 and change.

411
00:47:44,417 --> 00:47:53,966
So not a lot, but it all has to do with per pupil expenditures and things that are, Dave, I'm sure understands all this, but I'm still learning.

412
00:47:54,487 --> 00:47:57,410
Bottom line is that that is another income source for us.

413
00:47:57,550 --> 00:48:03,917
So what I've been able to do is take that money and put it into an account, and I'm able to use that to put right back into the school for the many projects we did this year.

414
00:48:04,557 --> 00:48:12,422
So with that said, I do know that I have some money available, and I do have some revolving lines that are now making some money again as we open back up.

415
00:48:13,903 --> 00:48:19,026
So what we're looking for is two additional instructors this year.

416
00:48:19,626 --> 00:48:21,688
Health assisting, this will actually be a third teacher.

417
00:48:21,708 --> 00:48:29,493
So if you remember correctly, last year, I asked for a third teacher in electrical and construction, and we did receive those teachers.

418
00:48:29,533 --> 00:48:30,653
So that's been helpful.

419
00:48:30,893 --> 00:48:32,835
Those are two of our most popular programs.

420
00:48:33,515 --> 00:48:38,639
Health and health assisting we're going to be able now to take in a few more students, but really this third instructor.

421
00:48:39,480 --> 00:48:46,705
is allowing us to be able to do our clinical rotations in a more efficient manner right now with two teachers, one that teaches freshmen and sophomores.

422
00:48:47,466 --> 00:48:51,870
it's difficult when the upper class teacher wants to be out with the upper class students two issues happen.

423
00:48:52,887 --> 00:48:54,728
One, sometimes we don't have enough room in the van.

424
00:48:55,688 --> 00:48:59,229
And two, sometimes we don't have enough coverage for the students that are coming in later in the day.

425
00:48:59,710 --> 00:49:09,653
So a third teacher would be able to work really with the upper class teacher for clinical rotations, drive the second van, be available for students that may not be ready to go out.

426
00:49:10,214 --> 00:49:18,257
So the rationale for that is that this is a popular program and we need to make sure that we have enough coverage for these students while also keeping in mind

427
00:49:19,057 --> 00:49:33,382
not all students can go out on clinical rotation, it's a 12 to 1 ratio, so sometimes we're balancing, you know, one group will go over to Winchester Rehab, you know, Monday, Wednesday, another Tuesday, Thursday, and it gets a little confusing and it's not really ideal, so that's why we're asking for that.

428
00:49:34,917 --> 00:49:39,763
The second position is a teaching assistant position, which would be similar in pay to Kids' Corner.

429
00:49:40,864 --> 00:49:44,168
I have reached out to our finance department just to find out what that pays.

430
00:49:44,989 --> 00:49:46,351
It will not be a full-time teacher.

431
00:49:46,391 --> 00:49:49,374
They do not need to be vocational instructor certified.

432
00:49:49,895 --> 00:49:52,678
This is specifically for our Make Way for Kids program.

433
00:49:52,698 --> 00:49:54,500
So in our early childhood education program,

434
00:49:55,724 --> 00:50:02,888
We, we have seen kind of a plateau, if you will, of student enrollment for high school.

435
00:50:03,588 --> 00:50:11,552
So we changed some things this year, I have the upper class teacher bringing the students out to the Brooks Elementary School launch and learn and creative corner.

436
00:50:13,001 --> 00:50:16,524
The success at the Brooks School, it's been amazing.

437
00:50:16,804 --> 00:50:17,785
The teachers have enjoyed them.

438
00:50:17,965 --> 00:50:25,492
So really, the students are working in the kindergarten classroom and the pre-kindergarten classroom, because I wanted the upper class students to get more experience above and beyond a daycare setting.

439
00:50:26,053 --> 00:50:28,575
If a student wants to get a job at Bright Horizons, that's fine.

440
00:50:28,615 --> 00:50:30,537
But I want people to remember that you can be a teacher.

441
00:50:30,597 --> 00:50:32,859
But part of this program is also to teach you

442
00:50:34,360 --> 00:50:36,162
you know, how to be an early education educator.

443
00:50:36,642 --> 00:50:41,025
So that has gone well, thanks to Suzanne Galluzzi for her support on that.

444
00:50:42,006 --> 00:50:51,674
So the teaching assistant is really just going to be someone who's in the classroom here within the high school for the Make Way for Kids preschool program that operates three days a week in the morning, two days a week in the afternoon.

445
00:50:52,454 --> 00:50:58,179
That allows the freshmen and the sophomore students to have some experience with kids because they don't leave the building for that.

446
00:50:59,680 --> 00:51:01,962
Questions on the instructor positions before I move on?

447
00:51:05,013 --> 00:51:05,373
Awesome.

448
00:51:06,093 --> 00:51:08,454
I'm also asking for an increase in three of our lines.

449
00:51:08,514 --> 00:51:10,355
And this is a direct result of two things.

450
00:51:10,715 --> 00:51:14,677
One, the cost of materials, as everyone knows, has gone up tremendously.

451
00:51:15,257 --> 00:51:16,298
And two, the enrollment.

452
00:51:16,798 --> 00:51:20,639
So we were able to get by because we didn't spend some of our revolving funds during the pandemic.

453
00:51:20,679 --> 00:51:23,080
So we've now depleted those lines.

454
00:51:23,321 --> 00:51:33,585
And after my budget analysis, I realized that without an extra $75,000 in my regular operating budget, I won't be able to provide the same level of service that we've done in the past.

455
00:51:34,285 --> 00:51:38,488
So I'm looking for a $50,000 increase due to the rise in enrollment under instructional supplies.

456
00:51:38,508 --> 00:51:45,394
I'm looking for an additional $10,000 in the textbook line for online subscriptions and online textbooks.

457
00:51:46,154 --> 00:51:50,137
And I'm looking for an additional $15,000 in our instructional equipment line.

458
00:51:53,020 --> 00:51:54,641
Any questions on those items?

459
00:51:57,143 --> 00:51:57,623
Thank you, Joe.

460
00:51:57,643 --> 00:52:02,147
Dr. Cushing, have we got it?

461
00:52:02,267 --> 00:52:02,827
Oh, it's me.

462
00:52:02,887 --> 00:52:03,127
Sorry.

463
00:52:08,566 --> 00:52:09,947
So thank you, Mr. Fallon.

464
00:52:10,387 --> 00:52:23,456
And again, as we mentioned last night, the vocational program is unique, both from a funding perspective, as well as from a programmatic one.

465
00:52:23,476 --> 00:52:32,142
And due to the consistency of the advocacy that we heard from the committee related to making sure that we're keeping a close eye on

466
00:52:34,965 --> 00:52:38,127
on those programs and making sure that we're expanding in a responsible way.

467
00:52:38,668 --> 00:52:45,292
The committee is also familiar with the district's statement of interest that was recently submitted to the MSBA.

468
00:52:45,893 --> 00:52:58,061
And I imagine that you can infer, but you can more than infer from that application, the extent to which we know that we need to make sure that our infrastructure

469
00:52:58,806 --> 00:53:06,570
is consistent with the needs of students and with the educational objectives of our flagship school.

470
00:53:07,630 --> 00:53:11,552
And so that made up a large part of that application.

471
00:53:11,612 --> 00:53:19,016
And I would imagine would make up a large part of the school's educational identity, excuse me, going forward.

472
00:53:19,056 --> 00:53:23,838
So when we go back to the main deck,

473
00:53:24,762 --> 00:53:29,185
Dr. Cushing, there's a couple other quick points related to the categorization of the vocational priorities.

474
00:53:29,225 --> 00:53:35,230
But before we let Mr. Fallon go, are there any questions from the committee for Chad?

475
00:53:37,311 --> 00:53:37,712
Mayor?

476
00:53:40,353 --> 00:53:41,314
Yes, Member McLaughlin.

477
00:53:41,754 --> 00:53:42,215
Thank you.

478
00:53:42,995 --> 00:53:43,836
Thank you, Mr. Fallon.

479
00:53:43,856 --> 00:53:47,619
It's always good to hear from you, hear about your success of your programs.

480
00:53:48,019 --> 00:53:48,579
Great school.

481
00:53:49,040 --> 00:53:49,360
Thank you.

482
00:53:50,585 --> 00:54:01,096
And toward that end, I was wondering if the ECE, if there's an opportunity or are there any ideas for expansion on that program to our other, any of our other elementary schools?

483
00:54:01,136 --> 00:54:06,221
I think, you know, to that point, there are so many opportunities for this program to grow.

484
00:54:06,302 --> 00:54:07,503
And I know that you said it plateaued.

485
00:54:08,063 --> 00:54:10,466
So do you think there's an opportunity for that in the future?

486
00:54:10,506 --> 00:54:13,409
Just wondering as it's, you know, being raised, it sounds like a great program.

487
00:54:14,516 --> 00:54:15,497
Yeah, absolutely.

488
00:54:16,057 --> 00:54:19,279
Shannon Deimos has been great this year because they were really our pilot school.

489
00:54:20,140 --> 00:54:24,763
But we started back in, maybe it was December, January.

490
00:54:25,364 --> 00:54:29,227
And I now have the schools asking me, how can we make this a permanent thing for next year?

491
00:54:29,287 --> 00:54:30,948
How can we make this a co-op opportunity?

492
00:54:31,488 --> 00:54:34,190
So yeah, there's definitely possibilities.

493
00:54:34,230 --> 00:54:35,271
And the students love it too.

494
00:54:35,371 --> 00:54:36,432
So it's been really fun.

495
00:54:36,812 --> 00:54:39,514
So I envision next year us entering two more elementary schools.

496
00:54:39,534 --> 00:54:41,235
So the good news is we do have

497
00:54:42,256 --> 00:54:44,058
enough upper class students right now.

498
00:54:44,278 --> 00:54:49,723
My fear is that like right now we only have three students as freshmen who chose it for sophomore year.

499
00:54:50,223 --> 00:54:54,287
That'll change a little bit, you know, some people might start the year next year and realize they want to change.

500
00:54:55,087 --> 00:55:02,394
The sophomores wouldn't be going out anyways, but we do still, you know, we have a healthy amount of rising juniors and seniors that will definitely keep this up.

501
00:55:03,315 --> 00:55:03,635
Thank you.

502
00:55:03,675 --> 00:55:18,463
And I would also just, if I may suggest, you know, partnership with or discussion with Mrs. Bowen's team as well, just particularly I think of people who might be interested in early intervention or other, you know, sort of aspects of special education on that realm.

503
00:55:18,523 --> 00:55:22,165
So I think it'd be interesting to look at that opportunity.

504
00:55:22,306 --> 00:55:23,426
So thank you so much.

505
00:55:23,886 --> 00:55:24,487
You're welcome.

506
00:55:24,727 --> 00:55:25,147
Thank you.

507
00:55:26,548 --> 00:55:28,649
Mayor, I just wanted to comment also.

508
00:55:29,429 --> 00:55:30,110
Yes, member Kretz.

509
00:55:30,538 --> 00:55:52,327
Yes, I just wanted to say I went to the open house and Sharon was there as well and it was so wonderful to see all the programs and it's just, it was phenomenal and I got to see some of the new skills capital equipment, you know firsthand, and it's just really amazing and all the great things and

510
00:55:53,448 --> 00:55:58,091
The students were there and they were showing some projects and it's just so wonderful.

511
00:55:58,872 --> 00:56:03,435
I'm so happy to hear about the increase in the enrollment.

512
00:56:03,995 --> 00:56:07,378
It's wonderful and it's a great opportunity for everybody.

