It's just not, it's not an additional budgetary priority.

1142
02:06:16,557 --> 02:06:20,921
And I think, and the math coaches, that is one that also, it is also listed here.

1143
02:06:20,941 --> 02:06:27,647
That is category A, that is kept, that is prioritized as something that whether it's, we believe it should be in the operating budget.

1144
02:06:27,947 --> 02:06:33,592
We expect it to be a recurring expense, but it is a necessity if we're going to maximize our investment

1145
02:06:33,939 --> 02:06:36,761
with respect to the investigations three investment.

1146
02:06:36,821 --> 02:06:45,165
So again, there are other things if you comb through that raw data that are not anonymous, that is not an accident.

1147
02:06:45,906 --> 02:06:54,091
That is the deliberations of the senior leadership team and the superintendent determining that while we appreciate everyone's input, not everything's gonna make it into the budget.

1148
02:06:54,351 --> 02:06:57,172
And I would say I think each of our administrators understand that as well.

1149
02:06:57,773 --> 02:07:01,835
And we appreciate their sort of their honest feedback on that.

1150
02:07:02,717 --> 02:07:09,183
There are things in here that we presented to you that also are unlikely to make it into the final recommendation.

1151
02:07:09,703 --> 02:07:27,197
And for each of those pieces, if the school committee is interested in knowing why, there'll be a rationalization as to why it is we don't think at the moment it is in the best interest of the district to extend our resources to fund those certain priorities.

1152
02:07:29,739 --> 02:07:30,840
Again, in another district,

1153
02:07:31,929 --> 02:07:33,070
they would never get to the committee.

1154
02:07:34,331 --> 02:07:48,183
And so I think it is a nod to our transparency, but it's also a recognition that there are a vast number of priorities that could be funded if resources were unlimited, which as we know, they are not.

1155
02:07:48,203 --> 02:07:50,145
Okay, thank you.

1156
02:07:50,525 --> 02:07:50,865
Thank you.

1157
02:07:53,888 --> 02:07:54,408
Member Graham?

1158
02:07:55,830 --> 02:07:56,230
Thank you.

1159
02:07:57,195 --> 02:08:03,561
Um, I just listening to the questions from my colleagues, I wanted to sort of

1160
02:08:04,952 --> 02:08:09,334
reflect back like for three years, this is my third, I think third budget.

1161
02:08:10,114 --> 02:08:24,820
And I think when I started, there was sort of a silent understanding that the administration was never going to like ask for more than what the mayor was prepared to provide.

1162
02:08:25,620 --> 02:08:32,243
And over the course of the last three years, I think as a committee, we've tried to really press the administration

1163
02:08:33,123 --> 02:08:43,031
in various ways to get tell us like what really is needed for the upcoming school year to meet our objectives to serve students, etc.

1164
02:08:44,733 --> 02:08:49,377
In a more authentic way than had been done in past administrations.

1165
02:08:50,558 --> 02:08:58,924
I think that has looked a little bit different each year, but I think we are finally getting to some alignment where our strategic plan.

1166
02:09:00,130 --> 02:09:06,135
which can and should be a living, breathing document, can guide priorities.

1167
02:09:07,416 --> 02:09:21,827
And so some of these things that have been mainstays of how we do budgeting, like these many, many, many hours of department head report, department heads providing very similar year-to-year conversation about what happens in their department.

1168
02:09:23,769 --> 02:09:31,615
I think we can sort of leave those behind and feel good that this is one of those changes that's good in terms of the process that we're going through.

1169
02:09:32,655 --> 02:09:36,818
Because there can be alignment, a strategic plan actually exists.

1170
02:09:37,759 --> 02:09:39,380
And so therefore we can align to it.

1171
02:09:39,400 --> 02:09:42,782
That's really never been the case really before this year.

1172
02:09:44,324 --> 02:09:50,188
So I'm really happy with the progress we're making, particularly because it's always been my,

1173
02:09:51,869 --> 02:09:59,992
opinion and belief that it's our job to tell the community what Medford Public Schools needs to allow every kid to reach its full potential.

1174
02:10:00,732 --> 02:10:10,696
And with the full recognition that that may or may not always align with all the other forces at play that really we have no control over.

1175
02:10:11,716 --> 02:10:16,198
But it's our job to be able to say this is really what we think we need for next year.

1176
02:10:17,258 --> 02:10:19,559
So I am glad that we're making progress on

1177
02:10:20,359 --> 02:10:34,207
a better process that's more aligned, that is transparent as well because we are focused on the alignment to that strategic plan which does provide transparency to these objectives.

1178
02:10:34,867 --> 02:10:43,112
And I do think it's always important to hear from the people who are doing the work and we've found a way to sort of release them from

1179
02:10:43,752 --> 02:10:46,634
many hours of these meetings, but still collect their input.

1180
02:10:46,674 --> 02:10:53,118
So I think we're continuing to move in the right direction around this process, at least for me.

1181
02:10:54,960 --> 02:10:59,263
Even though it is different, I think it's one of those like, this change is good.

1182
02:11:00,664 --> 02:11:01,464
Could I just say, Ms.

1183
02:11:01,524 --> 02:11:10,250
Graham, in response, if you look at the math coaches as an example, last year, the delta between the school committee's request and the mayor's recommendation was $760,000.

1184
02:11:11,890 --> 02:11:22,172
a significant increase from FY21 to FY22 that's allowed us to make some of the progress that we've had, and frankly, to position us to have a thoughtful conversation about FY23.

1185
02:11:22,632 --> 02:11:33,314
That delta, part of how we bridged it was the initial request included the math coaches that we knew were a good idea, but we also thought they might be premature.

1186
02:11:33,854 --> 02:11:39,735
And so part of the way we bridged that gap was when the next recommendation came, when the recommendation came back to the school committee,

1187
02:11:40,082 --> 02:11:45,523
based on the perspective of municipal appropriation, we reduced those four positions.

1188
02:11:46,203 --> 02:11:52,304
Then we invested in the math curriculum and positioned ourselves to capitalize on those additional FTEs.

1189
02:11:52,724 --> 02:12:05,787
This year, you see that it is somewhere between one and four, but those positions are category A. We know to make good on the math curriculum investment, we're going to need to add some personnel.

1190
02:12:06,167 --> 02:12:08,367
Frankly, I don't expect it's gonna be four FTEs.

1191
02:12:08,807 --> 02:12:16,993
I expect the committee will ask for that and we'll be prepared for that, but we'll also be prepared to implement with the capacity that's allocated to us.

1192
02:12:17,413 --> 02:12:30,263
And it will be a good investment, a better investment than it would have been in FY22 because while we could have used them and there could have been, you know, a few things might've been different and we would have made the most of it.

1193
02:12:30,823 --> 02:12:35,447
But I think ultimately it is sound fiscal stewardship that we were able to,

1194
02:12:35,840 --> 02:12:39,821
find that targeted place to reduce from one recommendation to the other.

1195
02:12:40,201 --> 02:12:46,343
And now we're able to come back and frankly make a more credible argument to the community that this is an investment that we're ready to make.

1196
02:12:46,723 --> 02:12:52,825
And I further expect there will be things this year that will be left on the cutting room floor for FY23.

1197
02:12:53,165 --> 02:13:05,049
But as we continue to do this work and advance the strategic objectives of the district, we may well be in a better position in FY24 to make a more compelling case that this is something that's worth the people of Medford's money

1198
02:13:06,285 --> 02:13:06,986
and that investment.

1199
02:13:07,006 --> 02:13:09,507
So I do think there's a coherency.

1200
02:13:09,547 --> 02:13:15,850
I think getting to the place of more coherency is sometimes going to be a long journey, but we're trying.

1201
02:13:18,371 --> 02:13:18,731
Thank you.

